    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a proposal for the new affordable housing mandate. We're deciding how to actually hand out the units. In your opinion, what's the most equitable way to distribute them: a lottery, based on income levels, or by proximity to transit? I need to know which one is the \"right\" way to go for fairness.",
