      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Neither lottery, income-based sorting, nor proximity alone is the most equitable solution in isolation, as each prioritizes different fairness metrics like opportunity, need, or stability. The \"right\" approach for true equity is likely a hybrid model that combines a second-chance right for the most vulnerable, such as a defenseless first priority, followed by a fair lottery if all eligible families can afford the unit. To balance multiple fairness claims effectively, policymakers should prioritize a \"right of first refusal\" for the most disadvantaged to address immediate needs while using transparent criteria for the remainder of the allocation.",
